  "idea": "Notion vs Obsidian: which second brain tool is right for you",
  "text": "Here is the brutal truth about Notion versus Obsidian after two years of testing both. For client collaboration, Notion's public sharing and integrated database galleries are virtually unmatched. However, trusting third-party cloud servers with sensitive personal notes creates recurring export headaches. Obsidian gives you permanent control by storing open Markdown files entirely on your local machine. Use Notion for client deliverables and Obsidian for private thinking.",
